# Human Benchmark++ currently requires NO API keys or environment variables.
# npm ci && npm run dev is enough to run the complete application.
#
# If you add a server-side integration later, put the real value in .env.local.
# Example placeholder only; this variable is not read by the current app:
# FUTURE_SERVICE_API_KEY=replace_with_your_own_key
#
# Never put secrets in NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables: Next.js exposes those to browsers.
# .env and .env.* are ignored by Git, except this example file.
